WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.350
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.250
Okay, Pikachu.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.260
We should finish up soon.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.150
We’re about to land.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.260
My first time in Kalos...

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.540
We’re gonna catch tons, Rabbifoot!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.780
You do your best
at the Battle Fest, Satoshi!

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.910
Yeah! I’m gonna win tons of battles!

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.520
Satoshi and Go
have come to the Kalos Region.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.680
Indeed...

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.030
To a town where a Gym Leader
with Lucario as her partner lives.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.370
Shala City, Kalos Region
To a town where a Gym Leader
with Lucario as her partner lives.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.030
Shala City, Kalos Region

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.940
There! I think that’s...

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.420
Kametete! Two-Handed Pokémon!
Rock/Water type!

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.890
They stretch and then contract,
yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops!

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.880
They eat seaweed
that washes up on the shoreline!

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.380
Monster Ball, go!

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.730
Kametete’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.880
All right!
Our first catch in Kalos!

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.490
It’s a Flabébé! Let’s go!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.870
Go!

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.390
This is the Grass Field!

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.630
The heated battle between
Pikachu and Bloster continues!

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.880
Bloster!
Luster Cannon!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.260
Pikachu!
100,000 Volts!

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:17.330
Unbelievable! Bloster’s enormous pincer
swallowed up the 100,000 Volts!

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:21.050
Electric-types should deal
massive damage, so how?!

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.950
What now, Satoshi?

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:31.710
PocketMonsters

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.130
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.710
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.430
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.300
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.640
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.310
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.810
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.070
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:01.660
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.580
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.330
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.340
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.550
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.890
Let's have a fight!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.600
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.430
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.770
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:39.440
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.780
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.280
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.410
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.210
I choose you!

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:02.220
VS Mega Lucario!!
A Battle Fest Bursting with Life!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.720
How’s that?! The power of Steel
can negate Electric moves!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.350
We have other options!

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.440
Iron Tail!

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.060
Crabhammer!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.820
Bloster!

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:33.460
Bloster is unable to battle!
As such, the winner is Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.560
All right! We did it, Pikachu!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.460
Satoshi, right?
I’ll remember that.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.470
This was Contestant Satoshi’s
third consecutive win!

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.660
If he wins his next battle,

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.990
he will breach the Super Class!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:57.260
The Battle Fest is a major event where people can rapidly
climb the ranks of the Pokémon World Championships.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.940
You are free to battle
whoever you want there,

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.170
making this one-day event extremely important
for trainers who want to enter a higher class.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.620
Monster Ball, go!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:18.120
Go!

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.010
I got Yayakoma!

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.270
Yayakoma’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.560
I guess we should go
cheer Satoshi on.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.020
Whoa! A red Flabébé!

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.830
We only need one more win to reach the Super Class,
and it’s all thanks to you guys!

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.590
Let’s give it our all
in the next battle!

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.630
Riolu!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.400
A Lucario...

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.740
Wait, could this Lucario be...?

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.240
Hey, Satoshi!

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.370
Corni! I thought so!

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.000
Long time, no see!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.580
I sensed Lucario’s Aura!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.520
How have you been, Pikachu?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.800
I’m Corni, a Gym Leader in Kalos.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.030
This is my partner, Lucario.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.880
You’ve caught a Riolu?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.060
Yeah! It hatched from an egg I got.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.690
I hope you’ll grow strong
with Satoshi.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.170
Satoshi and I had
an amazing battle once!

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.730
I won!

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.570
<i>That’s</i> what you're fixating on?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.590
It’s the most important detail!

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.080
Oh, geez!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.470
So, are you participating
in the Fest, too?

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:19.670
Of course!

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.330
But today I’m not fighting
as a Gym Leader.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:26.710
I’m a challenger trying to win my way up
the Championships to take down Dande!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.050
What?!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:32.300
Lucario and I are both doing this
to challenge ourselves.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.180
To train ourselves more
and rise ever higher!

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:40.710
I just have to win one more battle
to enter the Super Class!

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.390
It’s the same for you, right?

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:43.870
Let’s battle!

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.760
Whoever wins,
enters the Super Class!

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.190
Riolu.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.950
Watch Lucario’s battle
real closely!

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.570
That’s the spirit!

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.210
But just watch for today.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.760
Pikachu, look after Riolu.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.250
Anything here?

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.930
Can’t sense anything, huh?

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.710
Lucario?!

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.300
You have sharp reflexes.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.240
Its trainer?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.610
Sorry we got your hopes up.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:38.990
But I don’t think your greed
is a <i>bad</i> thing.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:42.170
I’m sorry.
I totally thought it was a wild Lucario.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:43.950
Is it your first time seeing one?

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:44.620
Yes.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.700
We came here to catch Pokémon.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.840
It’s my first time in Kalos,
so I wanted to catch tons!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.280
I see. How many have you got?

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.470
Oh, let’s see...

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.620
Quite impressive!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.720
You’ve gotten quite a few
Flabébé petal colors!

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:04.100
Catching an orange one
is particularly impressive.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.350
Now I just need the white one!

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:09.740
They say the white one
is particularly hard to find.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.320
I’m not sure they show up
around here.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.990
Do you know this area?

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.540
Well, yes.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:19.210
My granddaughter is battling
over there today,

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.620
so I figured I should come see
how she’s doing.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.290
The Battle Fest!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.880
My friend is participating there, too!

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.170
We came here all the way from Kanto!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.170
He’s here to battle,
and I’m catching Pokémon!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.680
Kanto, huh?
Haven’t heard that name in a while.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.750
My granddaughter is friends with
this trainer from Kanto named Satoshi—

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:36.710
Satoshi?!

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.430
Y-Yes, that’s right.
He’s partners with a Pikach—

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.300
That’s my friend!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:46.390
We will now commence
this Normal Class battle on the Rock Field!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.060
Contestant Satoshi VS
Contestant Corni!

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.070
This battle will be a 2v2.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.070
The crowd is going wild!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.700
It’s our very own Shala City Gym Leader,
Contestant Corni!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.200
Her opponent is Contestant Satoshi,
who came here all the way from Kanto!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.560
Let’s do this!

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.120
Oh...

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.370
You stay here.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.530
Hey, Riolu!

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.610
Cheer my Lucario on, okay?

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.890
We’ll show you
something really cool!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.040
What are you saying, Corni?

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.150
Riolu’s gonna be cheering for <i>us!</i>

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.990
Oh, there he is!
That’s Satoshi!

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.990
Well, this is a surprise!

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:37.350
His opponent is my granddaughter!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.530
What?!

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:41.460
PocketMonsters

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.330
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.620
PocketMonsters

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:52.540
Water
Rock
Kametete
PocketMonsters

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:57.140
All right, both sides send out
your first Pokémon at the same time.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.300
3!

00:10:58.680 --> 00:10:59.550
2!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:00.720
1!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.380
Go!

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:02.890
Come out!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:13.060
Kojondo! Martial Arts Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.630
It wields the fur on its arms
like a whip!

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:19.320
Its arm attacks come with such rapidity
that they cannot even be seen!

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.530
Kojondo... A real Fighting type
if I ever saw one!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.530
Battle, start!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:26.910
Acrobatics!

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.170
So quick!

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.500
The battle on the Rock Field has begun!

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:39.760
Kojondo’s blindingly fast Acrobatics attack
left Gänger no time to dodge!

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.260
Gänger, are you okay?!

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.970
U-Turn!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.810
Gänger! Psychokinesis!

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:54.150
Gänger!

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.030
U-Turn hits its mark!

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:05.530
Kojondo swiftly returns to its trainer
and switches out with Lucario!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.850
She used a <i>move</i>
to send her Pokémon back?

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.830
Yes. A fine call.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.760
Hang in there, Gänger!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.210
Bone Rush!

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.340
Dodge it and use Shadow Ball!

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.770
Gänger is unable to battle!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.360
You’re kidding!

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.450
Gänger didn’t stand a chance!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.320
Gym Leader Corni
does not disappoint!

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.950
A fluid combo attack
by Kojondo and Lucario!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.810
That was so quick...

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.600
Satoshi and Gänger
had no time to strike back.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.710
That is their strength.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.450
Corni and her Pokémon are as one.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.130
Therein lies her advantage.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:05.980
But Satoshi will still win, I’m sure!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.910
Come back, Gänger!

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:13.480
You did your best.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.810
Switch out, Lucario!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.480
Kojondo,
I’m counting on you again!

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:25.700
Contestant Corni recalls Lucario
and sends Kojondo back out!

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.670
Kojondo and Lucario
are both still unharmed!

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:32.120
Contestant Satoshi is up against the wall.
What is his other Pokémon?!

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.290
I choose you!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.010
Contestant Satoshi’s
second Pokémon is Kairyu!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.010
Kairyu! A worthy opponent!

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:47.830
Let’s go, Kojondo!

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.350
Dragon Claw!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.940
High Jump Kick!

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:05.490
They’re evenly matched?!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:11.490
Round-Trip Slap!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.540
Dragon Dance!

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:25.460
Kojondo’s Round-Trip Slap
is unable to stop Kairyu’s Dragon Dance!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.550
Quite the contrary...

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:31.100
It is helping the elegantly dancing Kairyu
to spin even faster!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:36.060
Dragon Dance is a move for powering up,
but he’s using it to neutralize Kojondo’s attacks!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:47.570
Kairyu has increased its attack
and speed with Dragon Dance!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.100
How’s that, Corni?!

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.240
We’re not done!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.070
High Jump Kick!

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.240
Dragon Claw!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.090
Kairyu pulls off
a swift counterattack!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.340
The effects of Dragon Dance
are clear as day!

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.970
Kojondo is unable to battle!

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:18.310
Great job, Kairyu!

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.400
That’s one win
for Contestant Satoshi!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.820
Now it’s one on one!

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:28.450
The key to his victory
was Dragon Dance!

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.570
Return, Kojondo!

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.620
You’re up, Lucario!

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:41.870
Satoshi! Battling you
really gets me fired up!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.090
Yeah! Same here!

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:47.250
I think it’s time you showed us
what Lucario can really do!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.930
Here it comes!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.760
Here <i>what</i> comes?

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:56.710
All right... Here we go!

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.600
Bursting with life!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.070
Mega Evolution!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.990
Mega... Evolution...

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.500
First time seeing it?

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:39.310
Yes.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:43.310
I knew it <i>existed</i>, but...

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.660
Mega Evolution is a phenomenon
first discovered in the Kalos Region,

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:49.860
that brings out a Pokémon’s
hidden strength.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:55.320
It is brought forth by a strong bond
between trainer and Pokémon.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.850
Don’t worry, Kairyu!
Just do what you always do!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.210
All right...
Dragon Dance!

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.450
Contestant Satoshi’s Kairyu
uses Dragon Dance again!

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.840
It’s increasing its attack and speed!

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:16.370
You’re being careful, huh, Satoshi?
That’s not like you!

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:17.220
Aura Sphere!

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.980
Fly around, Kairyu!

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:26.480
Kairyu throws Mega Lucario off
with its rapid movement!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:29.250
You’ll need more than that
to dodge Aura Sphere!

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.570
Go!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.740
Destroyer Beam!

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:41.290
A direct hit! The Destroyer Beam
didn’t make it in time!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.710
Let’s finish it!
Grow Punch!

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:55.880
Kairyu!

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.580
You okay, Kairyu?

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:17.470
Mega Evolution really is strong.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:18.630
What to do...?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.780
Kairyu! I have a plan!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:24.120
What?

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.750
Hurricane!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.250
Keep the Hurricane going!

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:39.470
Oh, my! An intense Hurricane
surrounds Mega Lucario!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:45.930
Is this even possible?!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.190
All right!
Just what I wanted!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.820
Here comes Satoshi’s craziness!

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:54.940
Now, Corni,
how will you fight back?

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.950
Lucario! We won’t give up!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.470
Aura Sphere!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.750
Mega Lucario successfully broke free!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.250
Grow Punch!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.760
Dragon Claw!

